  "description": "A dependency-free security toolkit for modern .NET, built entirely on RandomNumberGenerator — never System.Random. Cryptographically secure password generation (Generate, GenerateStrong, GenerateReadable, GenerateNumeric with configurable length and character sets), entropy-based password strength scoring returning a rich PasswordStrengthResult (score, level, entropy in bits, actionable suggestions), hashing (SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512, plus MD5 and SHA-1 for legacy interop) returning lowercase hex, token generation (URL-safe RFC 4648 base64url, hex, base64, GUID, and JWT secrets with a 256-bit minimum), and random utilities for strings, numbers, bytes, GUIDs and colours. Every generator uses rejection-free unbiased sampling, every public member is XML-documented and argument-validated, and the whole surface is covered by 550 tests on every target framework. Multi-targets net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0. Trim- and Native AOT-safe, with zero transitive dependencies.",
